WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.834
you know from shows
like "The Afterparty"

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.267
and "Love Life" and movies like
"Your Place or Mine."

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:09.367
She stars in "Party Down,"
which airs Fridays on Starz.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.667
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.601
-What's in these?
-Basic sheet cake

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:14.534
done in an on-sale,
store-bought style

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:17.167
with a center
of ripened camembert.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:18.434
-What?
Wait. What?

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.467
-You get an innocent
childlike sweetness up front

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.968
followed by an earthy whiff
of decay.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.968
-Why?
-It's a rumination on mortality.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.167
-Rumination on mortality?

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.801
It's cake.
-Birthday cake.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.634
-Please welcome to the show
Zoe Chao, everybody!

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:44.467
♪♪

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:48.000
♪♪

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.901
-Welcome to the show, Zoe!

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.234
-Thanks for having me!

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:54.467
-This is a very exciting
reboot of a show,

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.267
or I guess
it's an extension of a show

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.734
that came out 10 years ago,
"Party Down."

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:00.501
This is about artists
who work as caterers.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:04.701
You had a career, as did I,
in the food-service industry.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.434
-Yes.
-Did it bring back flashbacks?

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:07.601
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.367
I started to have
restaurant nightmares again.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.868
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:15.167
-Specifically, did I fire
the almond-crusted sea bass

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.300
for table 42?

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.367
Which I thought
I had left that behind.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.033
-No.
-But it was a triggering

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:25.100
and cathartic exercise
filming season three.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.067
-I had a longer
tale of nightmares

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.234
from being a waiter

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.167
than any other stressful job
I've ever had.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.868
-Truly.
-I still have -- did you ever --

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.200
What was the worst thing
that happened to you

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.167
when you were working
in a restaurant?

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.601
-Oh, man.
Um...

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:42.267
Okay.
Well, I accidentally fired --

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:46.367
put in -- four burgers
instead of four steaks.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.367
-Big mistake.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.634
-Huge mistake.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:52.767
-Pricey mistake that I would
have had to pay for.

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:56.501
I somehow intercepted
the food runner

00:01:56.501 --> 00:02:00.501
before he took the four burgers
to the table.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.834
And I was like, "You know what?
I got this.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.667
I really believe in, like,
continuity of service."

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:12.133
And then I had the four burgers,
and I was like, "What do I do?"

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:15.100
And the manager
was in one doorway.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.667
The chef was in another doorway.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.868
And the only -- my only option
was the valet entrance.

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.634
-Uh-huh.
-So, I took them out to valet...

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:26.300
-Okay.
-And I put them under a car.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.934
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.667
-And then I came back up.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:33.300
As I was coming back up
from putting them under the car,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.801
the manager had come outside
and was like,

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.567
"Yo, Zoe, what are you
doing out here?"

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:43.234
And I was, like, "Um...

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.033
Oh, I got gas."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.167
I got some gas.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:50.300
Didn't want to release it
in front of the customers.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.100
So just came out here
to do a little toot.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.300
Going back to work.
Going back to work."

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.534
-So, what was your plan --
long-term plan --

00:02:57.534 --> 00:03:00.133
with the burgers under the car?

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.767
-Well, three hours later...
-Uh-huh.

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:05.868
-...I went back out to see
if they'd been run over.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:08.501
And they miraculously hadn't.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:12.200
So, I took them out, I ate one,
and gave three to my co-workers,

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.200
and I've never had
a better burger.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.634
-Wow.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.534
That's amazing.
Do you --

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:19.834
And now when you make a burger,

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.367
do you leave it under a car for
three hours before you eat it?

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.734
-[ Laughs ]
-Just 'cause you like --

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.767
No, you're like, "It really
has this nice oily taste."

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:27.701
-Exactly.
No, but I should try that.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.467
-Now, you --
this is a show, again,

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:33.100
about artists who work
in the food-service industry.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.567
-Yeah.
-You were an art history major?

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:36.901
Is that right?
-I was.

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:39.701
-Before you became --
decided on the path of acting?

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.567
-Yes.
-So, what sort of things

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.367
did you -- was that
what you were pursuing?

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.300
Were you, like,
interning in that world?

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.667
-I was. So, my parents
are both visual artists.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.901
My sister is a visual artist.
So I thought, "Okay.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.501
I'll be an art history major,
and maybe I'll wind up

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.334
in a gallery or a museum."

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:58.801
So, the summer before
my senior year of college,

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:03.100
I worked for this
non-for-profit art gallery

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.868
on this project
called Karaoke Ice.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:11.033
-Okay.
-Which -- bear with me.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.734
It was a vintage car -- truck,

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:17.334
turned into
a traveling karaoke mobile.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:21.834
-Okay.
-M.C.'d by a mute squirrel cub.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:22.901
-Okay.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.634
-That would be played
by an actor.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.167
-Okay.
A human actor?

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.901
-A real live human actor.

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:29.334
-Dressed like a squirrel?

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:34.567
-Who would wear the squirrel
helmet and the squirrel tail,

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:38.400
drive the truck
into social happenings

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.634
all across L.A., like
the Hollywood Bowl, Chinatown.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:46.701
And then lure, without words,

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:48.968
people into
the back of the truck.

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:51.734
[ Laughter ]
-Uh-huh.

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.534
I'm really sorry I missed this.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:54.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.200
-With an ice pop.
-Oh!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.734
-So, there was a food component.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:01.334
And then --
And then you would --

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:05.701
Then, hopefully, the participant
would pick a song,

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.567
and it would be
a contemporary pop song

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:10.133
that was translated into
something called tinkle pop,

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:13.234
which is ice-cream-truck music.

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:16.400
So, if you picked, like,
Missy Elliott's "Work It,"

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.167
it sounded like...

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.634
♪ Doot-doot doot do,
doot-doot do do ♪

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:24.467
♪ Doot-doot do do
doot-doot doot-doot ♪

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:28.100
Yeah, so, I had
to hold auditions for two weeks

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.567
to find this mute squirrel cub.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.968
-So, what --
So you're holding auditions,

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.701
actors are coming in,
and you're having to explain

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:35.968
what you just explained to us.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:36.968
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.868
You think
I'd be better at it now.

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:41.033
-I don't think there's
a better way to do it

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:42.567
than you just did it.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.100
-Thanks, Seth.
-I think that was --

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.634
I mean, I think, at some point,
the artist might have to answer

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:49.567
some follow-ups, but not you.
-Right, okay, okay. Cool.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:51.400
-So, what would you look for
in actors who wanted to be

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.834
the mute school -- the moot --
the mute luring squirrels?

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.701
-Right.
Um, rodent tendencies?

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:59.067
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.400
-Like, I think -- I think --

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.968
I mean, well, I was, 20 --
-Yeah.

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:05.167
Right, you need to be, like, 40

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:06.901
before you know
what makes a good squirrel.

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:09.033
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:12.767
And so I --
Sometimes they'd ask for notes.

00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:17.767
And I'd be like,
"Um, more...rabid."

00:06:17.767 --> 00:06:19.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:20.734
So, I don't know, but we --

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:23.501
And then, finally, I was like,
"I could do this."

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:24.701
-Oh!

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.968
-I was like, "I could be
the mute squirrel cub."

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:28.100
-And did you?

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.701
-No, because I had
to go back to school.

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:31.300
-Gotcha.
But do you think this is

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.634
when you decided that maybe art
wasn't for you?

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:35.334
-Yes, Seth.
-Wow.

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:39.200
-So, I went home,
and I told my parents,

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.968
"I'm gonna be an actor."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.701
-Well, I'm sure once you
explained it to them like that,

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:47.334
they were like, "Absolutely."
-Yes.

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:50.501
-Hey, you know this obviously
is "Party Down," but I also want

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:53.901
to commend you for -- you got
to work with Reese Witherspoon.

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:56.000
-Oh, man.
-In her new rom-com

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.567
"Your Place or Mine."
How exciting was that

00:06:57.567 --> 00:07:00.234
to be a co-star with somebody
of her stature?

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:01.801
-It was too exciting.

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:04.067
It was kind of terrifying.
-Yeah.

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:07.834
-She's so dreamy
and has not aged.

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:10.701
So, I'm looking at the person
that I grew up with, you know,

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:13.834
who is just, like,
America's sweetheart.

00:07:13.834 --> 00:07:15.901
And every scene was with her.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:17.701
And I was terrified
the entire time.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:19.334
[ Laughter ]
Sweaty palms.

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:21.300
-Well, it certainly does not
show on the screen.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.033
And it's been so lovely
to have you here.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.167
Thank you so much
for joining us.

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:25.234
-Thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.234 --> 00:07:27.000
-You guys, that's Zoe Chao.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.968
"Party Down"
airs Fridays on Starz.

